=== INVESTIGATION ===

Web page (web/src/features/trips/pages/TripDetailPage.tsx, 89 lines) summarises ONE
saved trip behind a single source of truth — `useTrip(id)` → `GET /trips/{id}` →
`Trip`. The body is a four-tile stat row (Distance, Energy Used, Efficiency, Cost)
in a `Grid cols 2/lg 4`, followed by one `GlassPanel` holding a `KVList` of six
detail rows (Trip ID, Name, Started, Ended, Drives, Charges). `PageContainer`
carries the loading + error chrome; the body renders the success layout when `trip`
is present and an `EmptyState message={t('trips.detail.notFound')}` otherwise.

SI display contract (phase-42/48): `Trip` is SI-canonical — `total_distance_m`
(metres), `total_energy_wh` (Wh), `total_duration_s` (s). The page converts ONLY at
the render boundary:
  - Distance  = fmtInt(convertDistanceFromSI(total_distance_m, distanceUnit)) + unit
  - Energy    = fmtNumber(total_energy_wh) + "Wh"        (raw Wh, NOT user energy unit)
  - Efficiency= fmtInt(whPerKm[*KM_PER_MILE if mi]) + "Wh/mi"|"Wh/km"
                whPerKm = total_energy_wh / (total_distance_m/1000), 0 when distance≤0
  - Cost      = formatCurrency(total_cost)  (currencySymbol + fmtNumber(amount, 2))
  - Started/Ended = formatDate(...) (locale medium date; null → "—")

Parity manifest record (21 = 5 panels + 4 states + 12 strings):
  panels  : Distance, Energy-Used, Efficiency, Cost, GlassPanel5
  charts  : 0    maps : 0
  states  : loading, empty, error, success
  strings : 12 trips.detail.* keys (all present in the platform catalog as
            translation.trips.detail.* — see STRINGS note).

Hooks ported (web name kept at the Swift call site): `useTrip`.

NOTE — useTrip is web-`@deprecated` (the backend has no GET /trips/{id}; only the
list route is registered). Irrelevant to parity: this unit reproduces the PAGE's
shape + behaviour (the seam keeps the `useTrip` name and `GET /trips/{id}` mapping);
the live KMP client lands at P1/S2-S3 by swapping only the data-source body.

STRINGS note (binding): the 12 web keys `trips.detail.*` already exist in
apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings under the i18next default-namespace
prefix `translation.` (e.g. `translation.trips.detail.title` = "Trip Detail",
`…energy` = "Energy Used", `…notFound` = "Trip not found"). This is the catalog
convention every shipped sibling page uses (VehicleDetailPage references
`translation.vehicles.detail.title`; 278 `translation.*` call sites project-wide).
The unit therefore references `translation.trips.detail.*` so the literals resolve
from the catalog at runtime; the verbatim web key name `trips.detail.X` is preserved
as the suffix. No catalog edit was needed — all 12 entries are already translated.

COLLISION CHECK (single TeslaSync module): grep for `TripDetail` symbols/files
across apps/apple is EMPTY before this unit — no same-name type or same-basename
file exists (DriveDetail/ChargingDetail/VehicleDetail are distinct). Every type +
file here is `TripDetail…`-prefixed; the shared P2 tokens / P3 components / P1 Units
facade are REUSED (DRY), not duplicated.

=== IMPLEMENTATION ===

apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Trips/   (7 files, 758 lines; web = 89 lines — the
delta is the native model + seam + 4 explicit data states + SI/format projection
that the web gets "for free" from shared hooks/components; decomposed, not gutted)
  TripDetailModels.swift             TripDetailRecord (SI), TripDetailState
                                     (loading/empty/error/success), TripDetailDataSource
                                     seam (useTrip ← GET /trips/{id})
  TripDetailSampleData.swift         Sample / Empty(nil) / Failing sources + error →
                                     the 4 data states
  TripDetailFormat.swift             pure formatters (fmtInt/fmtNumber(·,2)/currency/
                                     date) + TripDetailStatKind (4 panels) +
                                     TripDetailInfoRowKind (6 rows) + display projection
  TripDetailPageModel.swift          @MainActor @Observable model: load()/refresh(),
                                     state projection, stats(units:)/infoRows
  TripDetailSections.swift           TripDetailStatsSection (adaptive 2→4 col stat grid),
                                     TripDetailInfoSection (GlassPanel5 + TSKVList),
                                     TripDetailSkeleton (loading)
  TripDetailPage.swift               adaptive scaffold + loading/empty/error/success
                                     switch + header subtitle + previews (4 states)
  TripDetailRouteRegistration.swift  TripDetailLink + .tripDetailDestination()
                                     NavigationDestination (web /trips/:id) + factory

Design notes:
  - @Observable `TripDetailPageModel` consumes the KMP-bindable `TripDetailDataSource`
    seam (loadTrip ← useTrip / GET /trips/{id}); the view holds no networking (ADR-004).
  - Single source of truth: `model.state`; every surface (stat row, detail panel,
    subtitle) derives from the `.success(record)` payload. `nil` → `.empty`
    (web notFound), throw → `.error` (retryable), in-flight → `.loading`.
  - SI only on the model; conversion at the SwiftUI render boundary via `Units`
    (P1/S5) + `@Environment(\.tsUnits)` (ADR-005). Nothing non-SI stored/computed.
    Energy is pinned to raw Wh and Cost to `$`+2dp, matching the web page exactly.
  - HIG-native + adaptive macOS + iOS (ADR-002/006): LazyVGrid(.adaptive) stat grid
    reflows 2→4 columns; GlassPanel uses `.regularMaterial` via TSGlassPanel (ADR-005);
    `.navigationBarTitleDisplayMode(.inline)` is iOS-gated; system back + ScrollView.
  - 4 data states are real surfaces (ADR-011): loading → redacted skeleton +
    ProgressView; empty → ContentUnavailableView (TSEmptyState, notFound copy);
    error → TSErrorDisplay + Retry; success → stat row + detail panel.
  - a11y: panel `.accessibilityElement(children:)`, header trait on the subtitle,
    VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type via Font.TS, dynamic Color.TS (light/dark),
    ≥44pt Retry target via TSButton.
  - i18n: every visible literal via Text/LocalizedStringKey resolving
    `translation.trips.detail.*` (web key names preserved); numbers/dates are
    device-formatted verbatim values (Text(verbatim:)), matching the web locale render.
  - Data source is a one-shot fetch (web parity has no live SSE subscription for this
    unit), so no >2-min staleness indicator is required.

